   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "〜わざわざ: expressly",
     "texto": [
      "To point out that someone made a special effort or took the trouble: **わざわざ きて くれて、 ありがとう** (thanks for coming all that way on purpose). It can express gratitude or, depending on the tone, reproach."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "わざと: on purpose",
     "texto": [
      "To say you did it intentionally: **わざと へんじ を しなかった** (I didn't reply on purpose).",
      "**つい** can indicate that something happened without intending it, but it isn't an exact opposite of **わざと**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "つい: without meaning to",
     "texto": [
      "To say you did something unintentionally and regret it: **つい ねすぎて しまいました** (I overslept without meaning to).",
      "It's usually used with 〜て しまう (lesson 038)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
